    "question": {
      ":question/id": "155e84fe-2e9d-58d8-a163-c5b9a45790b0",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y-z &=-8 \\\\ y-z &=- \\frac{15}{2} \\\\ z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that $z=4.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-(4)=- \\frac{15}{2}.\n$$\n\n$$\ny=- \\frac{15}{2}-(-4)=- \\frac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $y=- \\frac{7}{2}$ and $z=4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(- \\frac{7}{2})-(4)=-8.\n$$\n\n$$\nx=-8-(- \\frac{7}{2})-(-4)=- \\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=- \\frac{1}{2}$, $y=- \\frac{7}{2}$, and $z=4.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ - \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
